e local helix axis CA(i+3) - CA(i-3) over every helical residue, iterated to a fixed point. The seven-helix bundle dominates it.","A helical residue is axial when its local axis is within 55 deg of that normal. This drops H8 and the ICL2 surface helix, which lie across the membrane.","Maximal runs of axial residues, joined across breaks of up to 2 residues, are the candidates; a run spanning at least 25 A along the normal crosses the membrane.","Exactly seven survive in each structure and are named TM1..TM7 in sequence order. The build fails rather than guessing if the count is not seven."],"caveat":"These are the helical extents of these two models, not a canonical definition of the H2 receptor's TM boundaries: the same helix ends a few residues apart in the two deposits, which is real disorder at the helix ends, not an error."},"tm6_outward_swing":{"value_angstrom":10.41,"value_rounded_angstrom":10,"sentence":"On activation the cytoplasmic end of TM6 moves 10.4 A, measured between PDB 7UL3 and PDB 8YN3 after superposing their transmembrane bundles.","definition":"Distance between the centroids of the CA atoms of residues 230-233, the 4 residues at the cytoplasmic end of the stretch of TM6 present in both structures, in the common frame.","precision_note":"The lower-resolution map is 3.0 A, so this number is worth about 1 A: state it as 10 A, not to two decimals.","end_residues":[230,231,232,233],"tip_residue":230,"cytoplasmic_end_is_low_residue_number":true,"tm6_residues_common":[230,260],"lateral_in_membrane_plane_angstrom":10.16,"along_normal_angstrom":-2.27,"distance_from_bundle_axis_angstrom":{"inactive":7.35,"active":17.47,"increase":10.12},"helix_axis_angle_between_states_deg":19.17,"cross_check_helix_axis_angstrom":9.74,"cross_check_note":"The cross-check pairs no residues at all: it is the gap between the two TM6 helix axes at one depth along the membrane normal, so it is unaffected by the chimeric insert. It should agree with value_angstrom to about 1 A."